  "worked_solution": "We need to remove the radical $\\sqrt{49{r}^{5}}$ from the denominator. To do this, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{49{r}^{5}},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{16p}}{\\sqrt{49{r}^{5}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{16p}\\cdot \\sqrt{49{r}^{5}}}{\\sqrt{49{r}^{5}}\\cdot \\sqrt{49{r}^{5}}} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{16\\cdot p}\\cdot \\sqrt{49{r}^{4}\\cdot r}}{(\\sqrt{49{r}^{5}})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{p}\\cdot 7{r}^{2}\\sqrt{r}}{49{r}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{28{r}^{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{pr}}{49{r}^{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4\\cdot \\cancel{7{r}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{pr}}{7\\cdot \\cancel{7{r}^{2}}\\cdot {r}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{pr}}{7{r}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
